  "id": "COMPOUND:17374 - PROTEIN:4918",
  "verbalization": "Mollicellin N is implicated in the regulation of Fusion glycoprotein F0 through a series of molecular interactions. The evidence suggests that Mollicellin N acts as a target for multiple compounds, including 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and Patupilone, which in turn target Fusion glycoprotein F0. This indicates a potential pathway where Mollicellin N may modulate the activity of these compounds, which themselves are involved in the regulation of Fusion glycoprotein F0. The presence of multiple independent pathways linking Mollicellin N to Fusion glycoprotein F0 suggests a possible role in the physiological or pathological regulation of this protein. The integration of these pathways supports the hypothesis that Mollicellin N may influence the function of Fusion glycoprotein F0 through a mechanism involving the interaction with 3Beta-Hydroxyolean-12-En-23,29-Dioic Acid and Patupilone. The evidence is consistent with a mechanistic link, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the exact nature of the interaction.",
